## Security checklist (from the original catalog — don't skip these)

- [ ] Every tool's `inputSchema` is as narrow as it can be (no free-text
      where an enum would do)
- [ ] Any tool with real side effects is gated (see `ALLOW_WRITE` in
      `example_write_tool` if you included one) — off by default
- [ ] Anything hard to reverse gets a per-call `confirm: true` on top of
      the server-level gate (see stripe-mcp-server's `create_refund` in
      the original catalog for the pattern)
- [ ] Credentials use the narrowest scope/permission the provider
      offers — never a default full-access key/token
- [ ] Content returned by read tools is treated as **untrusted data** if
      it's ever fed back into further agent reasoning — guard against
      indirect prompt injection, don't assume tool output is safe
- [ ] Any network-fetching tool guards against SSRF if it accepts a
      user-supplied URL/hostname (see `fetch-mcp-server` /
      `playwright-mcp-server` in the original catalog for the pattern)

## Publishing to the MCP registry

1. `mcp-publisher init` in this folder
2. Confirm `name` in `server.json` matches `mcpName` in `package.json`
   (`{{MCP_NAME}}`)
3. `mcp-publisher validate`
4. `mcp-publisher login github`
5. `mcp-publisher publish`
